# Rimvio OS Constitution (locked)

**Canonical:** `docs/RIMVIO_OS_CONSTITUTION.md` · ADR-057 · `lib/rimvio-protocol/`

> Rimvio = **Identity + Context + Object + Intent + Capability + Platform + Protocol + Runtime + Permission + Market + Commerce** — not an app IA.

## Eleven pillars

Do not ship new OS features without declaring which pillar they extend.

## Locked separations

| Never | Always |
|-------|--------|
| `user.country` only | account · residence · billing · shipping · current |
| Platform = country | Core + Market Deployments (ADR-056) |
| UI route = Agent SSOT | Capability contract + index |
| Chat = Context SSOT | `RimvioContextEnvelope` paths |
| Parallel manifests | RIR → `rimvio.platform.manifest.v1` |
| Callout object = OS entity | `lib/rimvio-protocol/object-model.ts` |

## Intent routing

```text
NL → compileIntentFromUtterance → planCapabilityDiscovery → Platform Runtime → Commit
```

## PR reject

- New entity kinds without ADR + `RIMVIO_OS_ENTITY_KINDS`
- Cross-tenant data
- Auto Commit on payment / order / high-risk
- Per-platform commerce DIY bypassing `rimvio-protocol/commerce` contract
- Hub as file dump without discovery dimensions (country · trust · capability)
